    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>MARKHOR Block Addons ships a self-contained <strong>Container</strong> block that looks and behaves identically on any theme — classic or block:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Per-device flex layout (direction, justify, align, wrap, gap) for desktop / tablet / mobile.</li>\n<li>Boxed max-width or full width, per device.</li>\n<li>Padding, margin and min-height, per device.</li>\n<li>Border style / width / color / radius, per device.</li>\n<li>Background color, gradient or image — with light/dark colour pairs and optional lazy loading (Interactivity API).</li>\n<li>Box-shadow with dark-mode override.</li>\n<li>z-index / overflow / position, responsive visibility, semantic HTML tag picker, custom <code>data-*</code> attributes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>CSS is generated once at save time, cached in post meta, and printed inline in the head — zero front-end parsing.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin zip via <strong>Plugins <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Add New <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Upload Plugin</strong>, or copy the folder to <code>wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li>\n<li>Activate <strong>MARKHOR Block Addons</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the editor, insert the <strong>Container</strong> block from the <strong>MARKHOR</strong> category.</li>\n<li>(Optional) Configure dark mode under <strong>Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> MARKHOR Blocks</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20work%20with%20classic%20themes%3F\">\nDoes it work with classic themes?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The plugin ships its own design tokens, breakpoints and CSS generator, so it does not depend on the theme&#8217;s theme.json.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20slow%20my%20site%20down%3F\">\nDoes it slow my site down?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. Block CSS is generated at save time and cached; the front end only prints the cached, minified CSS inline. The lazy-background script loads only on pages that use it, as a deferred ES module.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release: Container block, save-time CSS cache, dark mode, lazy backgrounds, settings page.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "A collection of lightweight, customizable Gutenberg blocks — per-device layout, backgrounds, borders, spacing and light/dark colours.",
    "description": "<p>MARKHOR Block Addons ships a self-contained <strong>Container</strong> block that looks and behaves identically on any theme — classic or block:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Per-device flex layout (direction, justify, align, wrap, gap) for desktop / tablet / mobile.</li>\n<li>Boxed max-width or full width, per device.</li>\n<li>Padding, margin and min-height, per device.</li>\n<li>Border style / width / color / radius, per device.</li>\n<li>Background color, gradient or image — with light/dark colour pairs and optional lazy loading (Interactivity API).</li>\n<li>Box-shadow with dark-mode override.</li>\n<li>z-index / overflow / position, responsive visibility, semantic HTML tag picker, custom <code>data-*</code> attributes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>CSS is generated once at save time, cached in post meta, and printed inline in the head — zero front-end parsing.</p>\n",
